 "relevance_note": "Single-patient case study of Tangier disease with an ABCA1 variant: \"a TD patient with a unique mutation (C2033A)\".",
 "method_note": "Hand extraction of one patient (no script transcription of tables; Table 1 has the patient as a single column 'TD patient', quoted by row). Label 'patient' (rule 5). Relatives mentioned only as 'two second-degree cousins' (parents) and 'three girls' (daughters) were neither tested nor described as affected, so no rows. The 12 healthy control women are not patients; cohort_size_as_stated null. Thrombocytopenia and hypertriglyceridemia are read from Table 1 values against the paper's own 'Desirable range' column (117 vs 150-400 K/uL; 100 vs <150 mg/dL); the paper's text uses neither term. LDL 66 mg/dL is inside the '<130' desirable range, which has no lower bound, so low LDL is not reported. 'No enlarged tonsils' does not exclude the composite checklist item 'orange-colored or enlarged tonsils' (left not reported). Variant 'C2033A' is printed without c. prefix, so cdna_hgvs_as_stated is null; the protein effect is described only in prose (premature stop at residue 573), so protein_hgvs_as_stated is null. 'in both alleles' recorded as homozygous; parents' consanguinity stated but parental genotypes not reported. PAF metabolism measurements (enzyme activities, EC50) are research assays compared with controls and were not recorded as phenotypic features. No contradictions found.",
